Explanation: The bug in the original function is that it incorrectly identifies the tallest cabin as the one with a sea view. It should identify the cabins that are taller than every cabin in front of them, not just the tallest one.

```python
def sea_view_cabins(heights):
    # Returns positions of cabins taller than every cabin closer to the sea
    views = []
    for i in range(len(heights)):
        if all(heights[i] > heights[j] for j in range(i)):
            views.append(i)
    return views
```

